  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Activism (Ain o Salish Kendra) - ASK Strengthening Activism Towards HR Culture</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Strengthening Activism (Ain o Salish Kendra)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Interventionen M&#xe5;let &#xe4;r att avsev&#xe4;rt f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra                        m&#xe4;nniskor&#xe4;ttssituationen i Bangladesh. Programmets syfte &#xe4;r att bidra till inr&#xe4;ttandet av ett icke-diskriminerande och demokratiskt         samh&#xe4;lle d&#xe4;r v&#xe4;rdighet, grundl&#xe4;ggande fri-och r&#xe4;ttigheter f&#xf6;r alla    medborgare garanteras. Den totala programbudgeten &#xe4;r cirka MSEK 67,0. Sveriges engagemang &#xe4;r cirka 14,3%.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention objective is to significantly improve the human      rights situation in Bangladesh. The programme aims to contribute to   the establishment of a non-discriminatory and democratic society      where dignity, fundamental freedom and rights of all citizens are     guaranteed. The total programme budget  is approximately MSEK 67,0.   Sweden&apos;s commitment constitutes roughly 14.3%.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention objective is to significantly improve the human rights situation in Bangladesh. Through the programme, ASK aims to contribute to the establishment of a non-discriminatory and democratic society where dignity, fundamental freedom and rights of all citizens are guaranteed in compliance with the Universal Declaration of Human Rights (UDHR), Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination against Women (CEDAW) and the Constitution of Bangladesh. The successful implementation of the programme will have a positive impact on survivors of human rights violation, especially women and children. In the long run, it will substantially contribute to improving the overall human rights situation in Bangladesh.This programme will particularly focus on women, while other groups to be targeted include working girls and boys, ethnic and religious minorities, and survivors of human rights violations, human rights actors (defenders and duty bearers).The programme has been designed within the framework of the following specific objectives:1.By 2016, human rights standards and mechanisms are increasingly applied by the wider civil society.2.By 2016, access to justice for disempowered people is enhanced.3.By 2016, the accountability of the state to ensure human rights standards is enhanced.4.By 2016, the rights of working children are promoted.To reach these results, the organisation amongst other things will provide free legal aid and mediation services to poor and marginalized people; offer shelter and psycho-social counselling to victims of violence; run drop-in centres for working girls and boys; spread knowledge and raise awareness on human rights; facilitate community activism; monitor the human rights situation, conduct research; and undertake advocacy for law and policy reform and the promotion of international justice issues.</narrative>
  </description>
